# A record app.hedgeyour.fun -> VPS must resolve, and ports 80+443 open,
# before first `up` — Caddy needs the ACME HTTP challenge for the cert.
# Caddy auto-provisions and renews the Let's Encrypt cert.
app.hedgeyour.fun {
	reverse_proxy app:3000
}

# Container-internal probe, never published to the host. The healthcheck has to traverse
# caddy -> app to prove the public path works: on 2026-09-08 a caddy that failed to bind
# :443 came up attached to NO docker network, could not resolve `app`, and reset every
# inbound TLS connection — while its admin API on :2019 answered happily and kept the
# container "healthy" for 14 hours. Plain HTTP on purpose: busybox wget cannot send SNI,
# so an https probe to 127.0.0.1 dies on Caddy's cert selection, not on a real fault.
:8080 {
	reverse_proxy app:3000
}

# GlitchTip + Uptime Kuma live on VPS2 (ops/vps2/) with their own Caddy — monitoring must
# not share VPS1's failure domain. No monitoring ingress here on purpose.
